A||||18||Jncomutt||AHH!!  Smoke In The Car||||1||
Z||000000||Jncomutt||06-24-2001||01:04 AM||||Perhaps a previous problem that I left alone, I dunno.  OK well I'm driving on the highway today and I push the button for "vent" (I have an 84 w/AC)  After about 30 seconds, I smell something burning, and the smoke just starting pouring from the vents and the defrost vents.  I shut it off immediatly and pulled over (I had to, I couldn't see from soo much smoke)   The temperature slider was on cold this time too.  I don't know whats going on here. Anything I can first check out??<P>Also, does the air that comes through the vents go to the back of the car?  or is all the duct work under the front hood??  Reason I'm asking is because wondering if it could be sumthing in the trunk burning causing the smoke to come out the vents.  I have no idea...  Thanks again!!<P>------------------<BR>17 year old Fierophile<BR>'86 Coupe 160k miles<BR>'84 Mint Beauty 51k and original tires!||||reg||1
Z||000001||tgowens||06-24-2001||01:10 AM||||are you sure it was smoke?? If it was humid there today and there was condensation in the system it will blow out the vents when you turn on the A/C.........||||reg||1
Z||000002||LZeitgeist||06-24-2001||01:43 AM||||All of the vent ducting is between the base of the windshield and the vents - nothing goes to the back of the car. <P>If it was a greenish "smoke" (more like a haze), and it left an oily residue on the windshield, it was the heater core leaking antifreeze into the airflow. In that case, you would need to replace the heater core under the passenger side of the dash.<P>If it was actual *smoke* - as in the burning of something combustable - if you had turned the heat on, I'd think it was a bit of dried leaf or something that made its way through the vent system to the heater core. However, since you had the temp on 'Cool', I'm not sure what it could be, unless one of the vent control motors was burning out due to a jam of some sort... not really sure in that case...<P><BR>EDIT - typos<P><p>[This message has been edited by LZeitgeist (edited 06-24-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Mach10||06-24-2001||03:21 AM||||I hereby cast my vote for the "Iron Chef" Jncomutt, and his marvellous "Chilled Accessory Fan Flambe"<P>I'd say that the blower is cooking up a storm. Does the smoke smell "electric?" You know, burning insulation?||||reg||7
Z||000004||mrfixit58||06-24-2001||07:44 AM||||The vent is probably full of leaves. Pop the front hood and pull the fan. This will allow you access into the duct to clean it out. I've seen other Fiero in the bone yard that were there because of a dash fire that started in the A/C duct.<P><P>------------------<BR>Roy :D<BR>87 GT   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pennocksize.JPG"> ||||reg||4
Z||000005||Max The Chainsaw||06-24-2001||11:43 AM||||  I'd also go with the leaves or stuff in the heater cavity. there is a set of resistor coils (Look like springs on a circuit board) that control the speed of the blower motor. They get very hot on lower blower speeds and can set fire to dust or leaves in there. <BR>  Only other thing that would smoke thru the vents in cool mode would be the heater motor itself burninng out.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Jncomutt||06-24-2001||02:37 PM||||Hey thanks everyone, Gonna rip that thing apart later today.  As for Mach10, yes, it was actual smoke like burning electric.  I'm thinking the jammed fan.  Reason being when I switch from vent to defrost or heater (whatever causes the doors to open and close) I hear, and feel, a rustling of leaves and depris moving about.  I'll keep ya updated with the results.||||reg||1
Z||000007||rogergarrison||06-24-2001||08:48 PM||||yep, id say you prob have some debris in the vent and laying on the resistors for the blower motor. They get red hot.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Jncomutt||07-02-2001||12:35 PM||||Wow, won't believe what I found.  The fan and the white "blades" of the fan were PACKED with that insulation stuff.  I took the blades off, cleaned it all out, cleaned the motor insides out.  Thought it was good until I looked in the duct work of the vents.  All packed up as well.  I went to work removing handful after handful of the insulation until I got what I could.  After further investigation of the insulation I had removed, I notice a small little skeleton of what appears to have been at one time a baby mouse.  DAMN THING decided to make my fan a home I guess.  <P>When I was removing the insulation stuff from the vents, it was charred towards the passenger side.  <P>All I did was remove the blower and reach as far towards the passenger side through the hole as I could.  It felt as though there could be more debris in there.  My question is, how do I get to that area?  Do I have to drain the cooling system and take apart the whole frontal section?  Or, can I get to it from inside the vehicle?? Any suggestions quite helpful... Thanx again.  PICs of the packed insulation will be up soon!!||||reg||1
Z||000009||elfiero||07-02-2001||03:30 PM||||When I got my first fiero I had the strangest<BR>smell whenever I used the heater so I started<BR>to investigate and found a whole family of<BR>mice BBQ'ed on the blower resister!.It was<BR>not a pretty site. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif">||||reg||6
Z||000010||Phil||07-02-2001||08:30 PM||||Shove the hose of a shop vac up there and suck away.||||reg||1
Z||000011||fierohoho||07-02-2001||10:39 PM||||Another thought, if you have a vacuum that blows air, try and blow into the vents from inside the car and work the heater controls while you do it. That may help loosen and eject the debris out the fan hole.<P>------------------<BR>'84 SE 2.5l<BR>'85 Coupe 2.5l now getting a 3800<BR>'86 SE 2.5l||||reg||1
Z||000012||mrgone||07-03-2001||01:39 AM||||right after i vacuumed my car i noticed my vents were clogged<BR>"ill make quick work of that"<BR>not thinking i took off the vent and got in there poking with a pen on high speed fan.<BR>clean interior was soon full of pine needles and leaf bits.<P>dammit||||reg||1
Z||000013||overlord||07-03-2001||03:43 AM||||ewww....dead mice and mice crap.<P>had some mice make a home in there when i stored fiero for the winter.  Gawd awfull smell..almmost sweet smelling.<P>Good ol shopvac showed em whos boss.||||reg||1
